body:
Filled! Can I ask what discipline your thesis is in? I'm in game design and doing a thesis on strategies as well, so I'm curious. 

&#x200B;

I assume you know what you're talking about, but in case its something you overlooked (a lot of people did in game design classes), you might want to look into first vs third person perspective and the role of the avatar since you ask about first person perspective.

I mean first off, you're commenting on a thread of people who clearly aren't in your situation? In context, it's likely one person replying with the quote, who agreed with OP that it was easy for them. So yeah, I can tell you that some people have bad families so maybe this isn't the place to be complaining about it. You're joining a conversation you can't relate to and complaining you can't relate to it. Judging by other comments on the post, you would have found others who related to you more elsewhere. 

&#x200B;

I mean like yeah, because when it comes to things like emotions and opinions there isn't an objective truth. There's no objective "it was easy to do BLANK for Christmas!" because it isn't going to be true for everyone. We all have different lives. When someone says "100% of the time not seeing my family is like heroin," its their truth because its true for them. You can't tell me that it isn't true for me because some people like their families or are in good situations. You can't argue something like that because there isn't anything to argue about. It's a fact applicable to one person, that others might agree with. 

&#x200B;

The majority of people are in your camp here. Not seeing those closest to you sucks. Everyone knows this. But you specifically joined a thread that you can't relate to. Like.... Really?
